From: TODO Your Name <todo@example.org>
Date: Sat, 30 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: rawnand: qcom: add IPQ5332 support

IPQ5332 embeds the same QPIC block as IPQ9574. Upstream's ipq5332.dtsi
does not yet describe that block at all: unlike IPQ9574, there is no
"qcom,ipq5332-snand" node in mainline for this SoC, so this raw NAND
controller is added fresh at 0x079b0000 with no pre-existing devicetree
node to conflict with. Boards may instead wire that block to a serial
(SPI) NAND chip, in which case a future "qcom,ipq5332-snand" node would
be handled by spi-qpic-snand rather than by this driver; the Xiaomi
BE3600 Pro (RN01) is not such a board: it has a single 8-bit parallel
NAND chip on CS0, 4-bit BCH ECC with a 512 byte step size, which the
existing ECC_BCH_4BIT/ECC_BCH_8BIT capability mask already covers, and
is handled by this driver via the "qcom,ipq5332-nand" compatible.

The register layout matches IPQ8074 (device command registers at
0x7000, BAM at offset 0x30000, NAND controller part of QPIC), with one
difference: this is a QPIC v2 block, so the last codeword of a page is
described by the separate NAND_READ_LOCATION_LAST_CW_n registers and
the legacy EBI2 ECC buffer configuration register is gone. That is the
same hardware behaviour spi-qpic-snand relies on unconditionally for
the IPQ9574/IPQ5332 QPIC, so add a dedicated props struct with
qpic_version2 set instead of reusing ipq8074_nandc_props.

has_onfi_read_op is deliberately left unset: the driver then keeps
programming NAND_DEV_CMD1/NAND_DEV_CMD_VLD around the ONFI parameter
page read, which works on this block as well.

Signed-off-by: TODO Your Name <todo@example.org>
---
 drivers/mtd/nand/raw/qcom_nandc.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/qcom_nandc.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/qcom_nandc.c
@@ -2373,6 +2373,15 @@ static const struct qcom_nandc_props ipq
 	.bam_offset = 0x30000,
 };
 
+static const struct qcom_nandc_props ipq5332_nandc_props = {
+	.ecc_modes = (ECC_BCH_4BIT | ECC_BCH_8BIT),
+	.supports_bam = true,
+	.nandc_part_of_qpic = true,
+	.qpic_version2 = true,
+	.dev_cmd_reg_start = 0x7000,
+	.bam_offset = 0x30000,
+};
+
 static const struct qcom_nandc_props ipq8074_nandc_props = {
 	.ecc_modes = (ECC_BCH_4BIT | ECC_BCH_8BIT),
 	.supports_bam = true,
@@ -2413,6 +2422,10 @@ static const struct of_device_id qcom_na
 		.compatible = "qcom,ipq4019-nand",
 		.data = &ipq4019_nandc_props,
 	},
+	{
+		.compatible = "qcom,ipq5332-nand",
+		.data = &ipq5332_nandc_props,
+	},
 	{
 		.compatible = "qcom,ipq6018-nand",
 		.data = &ipq8074_nandc_props,
